@@ -0,0 +1,124 @@
+# Duranium on the Samsung Galaxy Tab Active3 Wi-Fi (SM-T570)
+
+Bring-up support for building and installing a postmarketOS **Duranium** image
+on the Galaxy Tab Active3 (`samsung-gtactive3wifi`, Exynos 9810), produced by
+the gtactive3-mainline Duranium track. This is a development bring-up, kept
+clearly separate from the regular pmaports/kernel track so the two can be
+merged later.
+
+## Pieces
+
+Local pmaports packages (branch `duranium-gtactive3`, under
+`build/wt/pmaports-duranium`):
+
+| Package | Where | What |
+|---|---|---|
+| `device-samsung-gtactive3wifi` | `device/testing/` | deviceinfo, kernel cmdline, USB-prep one-shot (clock gates + MAX77705 data switch), nested-GPT udev rule, watchdog/suspend/UI tweaks; `-initramfs` subpackage carries the early-boot bits |
+| `linux-samsung-gtactive3wifi-duranium` | `device/testing/` | prebuilt bridge kernel (src/linux `gtactive3wifi` + `drv/wdt`, bring-up `.config` + `duranium.config`) |
+| `duranium-usb-debug` | `main/` | the USB debug layer (separate package so release images drop it) |
+
+Duranium repo changes (branch `gtactive3wifi` worktree at `build/wt/duranium`):
+
+- `scripts/pmaports.py`: route a device's `-initramfs` subpackage and
+  `duranium-usb-debug-initramfs` into the mkosi initrd.
+- `contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/`: `build-kernel.sh`, `build-image.sh`,
+  `install-to-userdata.sh` and this README.
+
+## UI: phosh
+
+`phosh` is the default UI ("complete GUI"). Rationale:
+
+- The display is a 1200x1920 portrait tablet panel; phosh's scalable mobile
+  shell fits it, and phosh already has a Duranium integration subpackage
+  (`postmarketos-ui-phosh-duranium`, pulls `phosh-os-updater`), so OS updates
+  are wired into the GUI out of the box.
+- GPU is Mali-G72 with no Panfrost yet, so rendering is software. phoc is set
+  to the pixman renderer (`WLR_RENDERER=pixman`, via the device package) which
+  is far lighter on four Cortex-A55 cores than llvmpipe, and phosh is lighter
+  than Plasma Mobile under software rendering.
+- `plasma-mobile` resolves too (`UI=plasma-mobile contrib/.../build-image.sh`)
+  if wanted; it is heavier without GPU acceleration.
+
+## Disk layout: a GPT nested inside userdata (sda31)
+
+Duranium wants a whole GPT disk (ESP 1G, usr + usr-verity, LUKS root created
+on first boot). On this device that disk lives **inside** the Android
+`userdata` partition `/dev/sda31` (52 GiB, user approved wiping it):
+
+```
+UFS LUN0 (sda) ── stock Android GPT ── ... ── sda31 "userdata" (52 GiB)
+                                               └── nested Duranium GPT
+                                                   ├── ESP (1G, systemd-boot + UKI)
+                                                   ├── usr  A (erofs, dm-verity)
+                                                   ├── usr-verity A
+                                                   ├── usr  B / verity B  (first boot)
+                                                   └── pmOS_root (LUKS/ext4, first boot)
+```
+
+- **U-Boot** exposes sda31 as a whole disk via `blkmap` (the shared
+  `exynos-mobile.env` already maps partition 31 and runs `bootefi bootmgr`;
+  the gtactive3wifi board env must use that bootcmd, not the fastboot-only
+  override — coordinate with the u-boot track). It then boots systemd-boot
+  from the nested ESP and sets `LoaderDevicePartUUID` to the nested ESP GUID.
+- **In Linux** the kernel parses the outer GPT and registers sda31, but it
+  cannot partition-scan a partition, so the nested GPT is exposed with a
+  partitioned loop device. Two complementary triggers do this in the initrd:
+  - systemd's own path: udev's blkid builtin sets
+    `ID_PART_GPT_AUTO_ROOT_DISK_NEEDS_LOOP` when `LoaderDevicePartUUID` points
+    into sda31; `postmarketos-duranium-initramfs` already ships
+    `98-mark-subpartitions-workaround.rules` to re-arm the loop trigger for
+    non-optical disks, and `systemd-loop@.service` attaches it with
+    `systemd-dissect --attach` (partition scan on).
+  - our `90-gtactive3wifi-nested-gpt.rules`: also triggers the loop when udev
+    detected a nested GPT on the `userdata` partition
+    (`ID_PART_GPT_SECTOR_SIZE` set), covering boots without EFI variables.
+  Both pull the same `systemd-loop@<dev>.service` instance, so only one loop
+  is created. systemd-gpt-auto / repart / sysupdate then find the
+  `duranium_*` partitions on the loop device.
+- **Sector size**: UFS is 4K-logical, so the nested GPT is built with 4K
+  sectors (`deviceinfo_rootfs_image_sector_size=4096`); U-Boot's blkmap
+  adopts the UFS block size, so the sector size matches end to end.
+
+### Size
+
+The shipped disk image is only ESP(1G) + usr(5G) + usr-verity(0.4G) ≈ 6.4 GiB,
+well under 52 GiB. First boot's `systemd-repart` creates the B slot and the
+LUKS root and grows root to fill sda31, so nothing in the image itself needs
+resizing for the 52 GiB target. The installer only writes the image bytes.
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+# all heavy steps take the shared build/kbuild.lock themselves
+cd build/wt/duranium
+contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-image.sh            # phosh, edge
+UI=plasma-mobile contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-image.sh
+```
+
+`build-image.sh` builds the bridge kernel tarball, builds the three local
+.apks with pmbootstrap into `build/wt/duranium-localpkgs`, points
+`duranium/pmaports` at the worktree, and runs mkosi with that package
+directory. Output lands in `mkosi.output/samsung-gtactive3wifi_phosh_edge/`.
+
+## Install and first boot
+
+See `install-to-userdata.sh` and PLAN. Short version: boot the bring-up
+console, then
+
+```sh
+contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh \
+    mkosi.output/samsung-gtactive3wifi_phosh_edge/samsung-gtactive3wifi_phosh_edge_*.raw.zst
+```
+
+which streams the image into `/dev/sda31` over USB and verifies the SHA-256,
+then reboot into U-Boot.
+
+## USB debug layer
+
+`duranium-usb-debug` brings up the fixed-MAC NCM interface
+(`fe80::57:aff:fe00:1`), an unauthenticated root console on TCP 23, an sshd on
+22, and a kernel-log stream on 24 — all on the USB link-local address only,
+present in both the initrd and the booted system, enabled by default and
+disable-able (`systemctl disable --now duranium-usb-debug.target`, or ship
+without the package). Security notes in
+`build/wt/pmaports-duranium/main/duranium-usb-debug/README`.
diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-image.sh b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-image.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a0e602d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-image.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Build a Duranium image for samsung-gtactive3wifi from the LOCAL pmaports
+# worktree (branch duranium-gtactive3), including the local device, kernel and
+# usb-debug packages, without touching the upstream pmaports clone.
+#
+# Steps:
+#  1. Build the bring-up kernel tarball (contrib/build-kernel.sh).
+#  2. Build the local .apk files from the pmaports worktree with pmbootstrap
+#     into a package directory.
+#  3. Point duranium/pmaports at the worktree (so mkosi.configure's
+#     pmaports.py --skip-fetch resolves the device from it), and run mkosi
+#     with that package directory as an extra package source.
+#
+# Everything heavy runs under the shared kernel build lock.
+set -eu
+
+ROOT=${GTA3_ROOT:-/home/borysthebear/Projects/gtactive3-mainline}
+DUR=$ROOT/build/wt/duranium
+PMAPORTS=$ROOT/build/wt/pmaports-duranium
+LOCK=$ROOT/build/kbuild.lock
+PKGS=$ROOT/build/wt/duranium-localpkgs
+UI=${UI:-phosh}
+
+MKOSI=${MKOSI:-$DUR/scripts/mkosi-container}
+export MKOSI
+
+LOCAL_PKGS="
+	device/testing/linux-samsung-gtactive3wifi-duranium
+	device/testing/device-samsung-gtactive3wifi
+	main/duranium-usb-debug
+"
+
+echo "== 1. kernel"
+sh "$DUR/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-kernel.sh"
+
+echo "== 2. local apks -> $PKGS"
+mkdir -p "$PKGS"
+# Build each local package for aarch64 with pmbootstrap, using the worktree as
+# the aports dir. abuild computes missing checksums for local sources.
+for p in $LOCAL_PKGS; do
+	name=$(basename "$p")
+	flock "$LOCK" pmbootstrap -y --aports "$PMAPORTS" build --arch aarch64 --force "$name"
+done
+# Collect the freshly built apks (pmbootstrap stores them under its packages
+# dir); copy aarch64 + noarch into one flat directory for mkosi.
+PMB_PKGDIR=$(pmbootstrap config work)/packages/edge
+cp -f "$PMB_PKGDIR"/aarch64/*.apk "$PKGS"/ 2>/dev/null || true
+cp -f "$PMB_PKGDIR"/noarch/*.apk  "$PKGS"/ 2>/dev/null || true
+
+echo "== 3. mkosi image"
+ln -sfn "$PMAPORTS" "$DUR/pmaports"
+cd "$DUR"
+[ -f mkosi.version ] || "$MKOSI" bump
+IMAGE_ID="samsung-gtactive3wifi_${UI}_edge"
+flock "$LOCK" "$MKOSI" build \
+	--force \
+	--architecture=arm64 \
+	--image-id="$IMAGE_ID" \
+	--environment=PMOS_DEVICE=samsung-gtactive3wifi \
+	--environment=PMOS_VARIANT="$UI" \
+	--release=edge \
+	--package-directory="$PKGS" \
+	"$@"
+
+echo "Image in: $DUR/mkosi.output/$IMAGE_ID/"
+ls -l "$DUR/mkosi.output/$IMAGE_ID/" || true
diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-kernel.sh b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-kernel.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..55b4e63
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/build-kernel.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Build the Duranium bring-up kernel for the Galaxy Tab Active3 and package it
+# into the tarball that the prebuilt bridge APKBUILD
+# (device/testing/linux-samsung-gtactive3wifi-duranium) consumes.
+#
+# This is the bridge until the regular gtactive3wifi pmaports track ships a
+# from-source kernel package. It uses the SAME source and config that the lead
+# tests on the device:
+#   source : gtactive3-mainline src/linux, branch gtactive3wifi + drv/wdt
+#            (snapshotted at build/wt/duranium-linux by the Duranium track)
+#   config : build/bringup/.config + the duranium.config fragment
+#
+# Run under the shared kernel build lock, like every other heavy build here.
+set -eu
+
+ROOT=${GTA3_ROOT:-/home/borysthebear/Projects/gtactive3-mainline}
+SRC=$ROOT/build/wt/duranium-linux
+OUT=$ROOT/build/wt/duranium-out
+FRAG=$ROOT/build/wt/pmaports-duranium/device/testing/linux-samsung-gtactive3wifi-duranium/duranium.config
+PKGDIR=$ROOT/build/wt/pmaports-duranium/device/testing/linux-samsung-gtactive3wifi-duranium
+LOCK=$ROOT/build/kbuild.lock
+CROSS=${CROSS_COMPILE:-aarch64-linux-gnu-}
+JOBS=${JOBS:-6}
+
+[ -d "$SRC" ] || { echo "kernel source snapshot missing: $SRC" >&2; exit 1; }
+
+mkdir -p "$OUT"
+( cd "$SRC" && ARCH=arm64 scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m -O "$OUT" \
+	"$ROOT/build/bringup/.config" "$FRAG" )
+flock "$LOCK" nice -n 19 make -C "$SRC" O="$OUT" ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE="$CROSS" olddefconfig
+flock "$LOCK" nice -n 19 make -C "$SRC" O="$OUT" ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE="$CROSS" -j"$JOBS" \
+	Image modules exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dtb
+
+KREL=$(cat "$OUT/include/config/kernel.release")
+STAGE=$(mktemp -d)
+trap 'rm -rf "$STAGE"' EXIT
+
+install -Dm644 "$OUT/arch/arm64/boot/Image" "$STAGE/boot/vmlinuz"
+install -Dm644 "$OUT/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dtb" \
+	"$STAGE/boot/dtbs/exynos/exynos9810-gtactive3wifi.dtb"
+flock "$LOCK" nice -n 19 make -C "$SRC" O="$OUT" ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE="$CROSS" \
+	INSTALL_MOD_PATH="$STAGE/usr" INSTALL_MOD_STRIP=1 modules_install
+rm -f "$STAGE/usr/lib/modules/$KREL/build" "$STAGE/usr/lib/modules/$KREL/source"
+printf '%s\n' "$KREL" > "$STAGE/usr/share/kernel/kernel.release"
+
+TARBALL="$PKGDIR/kernel-prebuilt.tar.gz"
+tar -C "$STAGE" -czf "$TARBALL" boot usr
+sum=$(sha512sum "$TARBALL" | cut -d' ' -f1)
+# Refresh the checksum line in the bridge APKBUILD
+sed -i "s|^[0-9a-f]\{128\}  kernel-prebuilt.tar.gz\$|$sum  kernel-prebuilt.tar.gz|" \
+	"$PKGDIR/APKBUILD"
+
+echo "kernel.release = $KREL"
+echo "tarball        = $TARBALL"
+echo "sha512         = $sum"
diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..98181b2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/install-to-userdata.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+#!/bin/bash
+# Write a Duranium disk image into the Android userdata partition (sda31) of
+# the Galaxy Tab Active3, over the bring-up debug console, and verify it.
+#
+# The device must be sitting in the gtactive3-mainline bring-up console
+# (S-Boot -> uniLoader -> mainline Linux + nolibc init), which exposes the
+# "put PATH LEN" (host -> device raw stream) and "cat PATH" (device -> host
+# raw stream) commands over USB. This script uses the repo's tab/tab-put/
+# tab-get helpers, so the USB network must be up ("tab wait").
+#
+# Duranium lives in a GPT nested at the very start of sda31; the image is the
+# first ~6-7 GiB of that disk (ESP + usr + verity). First boot grows the
+# partitions into the full 52 GiB via systemd-repart, so only the image size
+# is written here, not the whole partition.
+#
+# Usage:
+#   install-to-userdata.sh IMAGE            # IMAGE is .raw or .raw.zst / .zst
+#   install-to-userdata.sh IMAGE --no-verify
+set -euo pipefail
+
+ROOT=${GTA3_ROOT:-/home/borysthebear/Projects/gtactive3-mainline}
+TAB=$ROOT/scripts/tab
+TAB_PUT=$ROOT/scripts/tab-put
+TAB_GET=$ROOT/scripts/tab-get
+DEV=/dev/sda31          # Android userdata, confirmed in HARDWARE.md
+IMG=${1:?usage: install-to-userdata.sh IMAGE [--no-verify]}
+VERIFY=1
+[ "${2:-}" = "--no-verify" ] && VERIFY=0
+
+command -v zstd >/dev/null || { echo "zstd required" >&2; exit 1; }
+
+# Decompress to a plain raw image if needed.
+case "$IMG" in
+	*.zst)
+		RAW=$(mktemp --suffix=.raw)
+		trap 'rm -f "$RAW"' EXIT
+		echo "Decompressing $IMG -> $RAW"
+		zstd -d -f -o "$RAW" "$IMG"
+		;;
+	*)
+		RAW=$IMG
+		;;
+esac
+
+LEN=$(stat -c %s "$RAW")
+echo "Image: $RAW ($LEN bytes)"
+
+echo "Waiting for the tablet's USB console..."
+"$TAB" wait
+
+# Sanity: confirm the target exists and show its size (in 512-byte sectors).
+SECT=$("$TAB" "cat /sys/class/block/sda31/size" | tr -dc 0-9)
+PARTBYTES=$(( SECT * 512 ))
+echo "Target $DEV: $PARTBYTES bytes ($SECT sectors)"
+if [ "$LEN" -gt "$PARTBYTES" ]; then
+	echo "ERROR: image ($LEN) is larger than $DEV ($PARTBYTES)" >&2
+	exit 1
+fi
+
+echo "Streaming image into $DEV ..."
+# tab-put opens the path for writing and streams exactly LEN bytes into it.
+# For a block device the create/truncate flags are no-ops; the bytes land at
+# offset 0, which is where the nested GPT begins.
+"$TAB_PUT" "$RAW" "$DEV"
+"$TAB" "write /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches 3" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
+
+if [ "$VERIFY" = 1 ]; then
+	echo "Verifying (reading $LEN bytes back and comparing sha256)..."
+	WANT=$(sha256sum "$RAW" | cut -d' ' -f1)
+	BACK=$(mktemp --suffix=.raw)
+	trap 'rm -f "${RAW##*/}" "$BACK" 2>/dev/null; rm -f "$BACK"' EXIT
+	# tab-get reads exactly LEN bytes from the device node.
+	"$TAB_GET" "$DEV" "$BACK" "$LEN"
+	GOT=$(sha256sum "$BACK" | cut -d' ' -f1)
+	if [ "$WANT" != "$GOT" ]; then
+		echo "VERIFY FAILED: wrote $WANT, read back $GOT" >&2
+		exit 1
+	fi
+	echo "Verify OK ($WANT)"
+fi
+
+cat <<EOF
+
+Done. The Duranium GPT is now written to $DEV.
+Next:
+  1. Reboot the tablet into U-Boot (the boot chain on BOOT), e.g.
+       $TAB "reboot normal"
+     U-Boot exposes sda31 as a whole disk via blkmap and runs "bootefi
+     bootmgr" -> systemd-boot -> the Duranium UKI.
+  2. First boot runs systemd-repart (creates the B-slot usr+verity and the
+     LUKS root, growing into the full 52 GiB) and then f0rmz for user setup.
+EOF
